:: LearnAboutBerries [childhood]
# Fruits of the Forest

"Which berries are good to eat?" you ask, pointing at the different piles being processed.

Your mother smiles at your curiosity. "This is important knowledge," she says. "Some berries feed us, others heal us, and some can make us very sick."

She shows you several types, explaining the differences:

"These red ones are sweet and safe, but these other red ones with a different leaf pattern will give you a terrible stomach pain."

"The dark blue berries are very good for you - they give strength during winter."

"These small black ones can help with coughing sickness."

You try to memorize the shapes, colors, and growing patterns of each type. This knowledge could save your life someday, especially when you begin to gather food on your own.

